preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: "From Monovalent Dev to Bivalent DevOps to Trivalent DevIntOps: Intelligence as the Third Continuous Loop in Software Engineering"
  authors:
    - family-names: Chertorogov
      given-names: Pavel
  year: 2026
  month: 10
  version: "1.0"
  url: "https://devintops.org/v1/"
  abstract: >-
    Finishing a task does not ensure that the next task benefits from it.
    DevOps already values learning; DevIntOps makes the state that carries
    learning into later decisions an explicit engineering responsibility.
    Development changes the implementation, Operations changes how it runs,
    and Intelligence changes how it decides. The third loop uses memory and
    judgment through Understand, Predict, Orchestrate and Learn. A pass
    connects a goal or outcome to a decision and evaluated experience. In
    engineering, that experience becomes a lesson with a source, a permitted
    change, an independent check and a way out. An escaped bug and a product
    decision show how the same logical pattern serves different systems.
    Evidence limits authority; people retain goals, permissions and scoring.
    The model combines established learning and adaptive-control practices
    rather than claiming to invent them. Its lifecycle-wide benefit remains
    untested. A randomized shadow comparison specifies what would count as
    improvement, failure or an inconclusive result.
